By Dr. Burt, a member of the National Association of Medical Students at
University of Washington (UMS)
As part of a special training program designed to help medical students gain knowledge and skills in how to use medical terminology effectively, this pilot project aims to make it easier for medical students to understand how to use medical terms.
The goal is to introduce medical students to the concepts they need to know. The goal is to allow them to practice various aspects of medical terminology such as:
- How to use the terms properly;
- How to use terminology correctly in medical contexts;
- How to use acronyms, abbreviations, and abbreviations;
- What are the risks involved with using the term?
“This pilot program will help medical students become aware of the differences between the terms that describe the concepts they’re learning and those that do not,” says Dr. Burt. “It also gives you the opportunity to learn more about what they already know.”
